## Defects found DURING integration (not in any lane's plan)

1. **The case page returned 500 in every production build.** `next build && next
   start` - which is exactly what the compose deploy runs - failed with
   `Could not find the module ... in the React Server Consumer Manifest` for
   every `/cases/...` URL, because the route declared `runtime = "edge"` while
   its client components are bundled for the Node server. Dev mode hid it, e2e
   never covered the page, and the compose stack had never been started, so the
   product's core screen was unopenable in every deployable build. Fixed in
   826bb93.
2. **The thinking trace vanished on a fast run or a page reload**, because the
   panel only consumed SSE increments and never read the persisted stream.
   Fixed in 4712fe7.
3. `DossierEntry.decision_case_id.in_([case_id, None])` silently dropped every
   subject-wide fact (SQL `IN` never matches NULL) - caught by the new
   subject-scope test before it shipped.

